{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25598482",
      "title": "Managing the Error State",
      "sourceHash": "b40492404166c4216f34afe64cf208423425f4adc18e3452e50a9fb949e98f74",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 4.78,
          "en": "So let's make sure we only show the error modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.78,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "if we entered something invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 10.45,
          "en": "So in the AddUser component, currently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.45,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "if we have an empty input or an invalid age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "we just return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 17.683,
          "en": "We cancel this function execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.95,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "I wanna continue doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.18,
          "en": "but in addition I also wanna show an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.18,
          "end": 24.41,
          "en": "in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.41,
          "end": 25.66,
          "en": "And therefore, we need a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.66,
          "end": 29.703,
          "en": "of dynamically showing and hiding this error modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.7,
          "end": 33.88,
          "en": "Put in other words, we need to update our UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.88,
          "end": 36.41,
          "en": "conditionally, based on the question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.41,
          "end": 38.403,
          "en": "if we have an error or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.34,
          "end": 41.96,
          "en": "And what does this scream for?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.96,
          "end": 43.03,
          "en": "State management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.03,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "We need to manage some error state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.71,
          "en": "and that could be a string like the error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.71,
          "end": 50.92,
          "en": "that could be an object which bundles error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.92,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "or title message, whatever you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "but we need to manage such an error state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 59.27,
          "en": "so that we can set it to, we have an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.27,
          "end": 61.51,
          "en": "in which case we wanna render the modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.51,
          "end": 64.25,
          "en": "and so that we can set it to, we got no error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.25,
          "end": 66.84,
          "en": "in which case we render nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.84,
          "end": 68.48,
          "en": "I mean, we still rendered a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.48,
          "end": 70.793,
          "en": "but we wouldn't render the modal in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.77,
          "end": 74.913,
          "en": "So we need an extra piece of state here, useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.7,
          "end": 79.3,
          "en": "and the initial value is actually undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.3,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "so I don't need to pass any other initial value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "between the parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 87.69,
          "en": "Now I'll name that error and setError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 90.57,
          "en": "because in the end I'm going to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 92.293,
          "en": "some error information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.22999999999999,
          "end": 95.25999999999999,
          "en": "And now again, it's your app, it's up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.25999999999999,
          "end": 98.22999999999999,
          "en": "how an error should look like for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.22999999999999,
          "end": 100.83,
          "en": "If it's just a string or if it's an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 103.47999999999999,
          "en": "I will manage an error as an object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.47999999999999,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "So here in that first validation part, I will call set error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.16,
          "end": 112.49000000000001,
          "en": "and set this to an object where I wanna have a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.49000000000001,
          "end": 117.28,
          "en": "like invalid input and a message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.28,
          "end": 122.28,
          "en": "where I say, please enter a valid name and age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.53,
          "end": 125.763,
          "en": "non-empty values, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 129.053,
          "en": "And this will set the error state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "Now I'll do the exact same here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 134.67,
          "en": "in the second validation function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.67,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "I'll change the title to invalid age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "because here we know that the age is the missing piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 142.35,
          "en": "and that the age is invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.35,
          "end": 145.16,
          "en": "and I'll have a different message as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.16,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "I'll have a message that says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 152.01,
          "en": "please enter a valid age greater zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.01,
          "end": 153.913,
          "en": "so that's my error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.35,
          "end": 158.25,
          "en": "So we set our error state in both cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 160.75,
          "en": "but we set it to a slightly different object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.75,
          "end": 162.82999999999998,
          "en": "in both scenarios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.82999999999998,
          "end": 165,
          "en": "The object always has the same properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 168.29,
          "en": "and that is important so that we can reliably use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.29,
          "end": 170.653,
          "en": "but the properties hold different values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 174.62,
          "en": "Now with that, that error state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.62,
          "end": 178.66,
          "en": "will hold that error, whenever we call setError,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.66,
          "end": 181.06,
          "en": "because then the entire component will rerender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.06,
          "end": 184.1,
          "en": "and error will hold the latest error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.1,
          "end": 185.523,
          "en": "as a state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.68,
          "end": 190,
          "en": "Hence, we can use that down there in our JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190,
          "end": 192.523,
          "en": "to conditionally render the error modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.63,
          "end": 197.32999999999998,
          "en": "We just need to check if error is a thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.053,
          "en": "and if it is, with that AND operator, we output error model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.227,
          "end": 206.7,
          "en": "Otherwise, if error would be undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.7,
          "end": 209.86,
          "en": "well nothing would be rendered here for this line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.86,
          "end": 213.623,
          "en": "And that is how we can conditionally render a JSX element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 218.65,
          "en": "We need wrapping curly braces around this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.65,
          "end": 221.7,
          "en": "because this generally is a JavaScript expression,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.7,
          "end": 225.263,
          "en": "just one, which then also holds a JSX element again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.92000000000002,
          "end": 229.73,
          "en": "So now the error modal will only be output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.73,
          "end": 231.13,
          "en": "if we have an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.13,
          "end": 234.61,
          "en": "And now since the error also is a more complex object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.61,
          "end": 236.35,
          "en": "with a title and a message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.35,
          "end": 238.6,
          "en": "we can utilize that title and message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.6,
          "end": 242.703,
          "en": "to output it as the actual title and message in our modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.83,
          "end": 248.83,
          "en": "So here I'll bind title to error.title and message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 250.33,
          "end": 255.33,
          "en": "of course, unsurprisingly to error.message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.91,
          "end": 260.41,
          "en": "And with that if we save this, we get nothing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.41,
          "end": 262.66,
          "en": "but if I submit an empty form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.66,
          "end": 264.14300000000003,
          "en": "you see here is my modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.04,
          "end": 267.61,
          "en": "Right now, we have no way of dismissing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.61,
          "end": 269.94,
          "en": "the button doesn't work yet, but we can of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 272.93,
          "en": "reload the page for now so that I also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 272.93,
          "end": 274.77,
          "en": "the invalid age case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.77,
          "end": 279.15999999999997,
          "en": "If I entered this, you see I get the invalid age error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.15999999999997,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "So that is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.95,
          "en": "That works exactly in the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.95,
          "end": 285.67,
          "en": "Now let's make sure we can also dismiss it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.67,
          "end": 288.21,
          "en": "by either clicking on the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.21,
          "end": 290.313,
          "en": "or by clicking on the Okay button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.97,
          "end": 294.07,
          "en": "Now for that, what we need to do of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.07,
          "end": 299.07,
          "en": "is we need to clear our error state, this error state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 301.75,
          "en": "because if we have an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.75,
          "end": 305.43,
          "en": "if what's stored in this state snapshot is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 305.43,
          "end": 307.65,
          "en": "which a JavaScript object is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.65,
          "end": 309.89,
          "en": "we'll render the error modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 309.89,
          "end": 313.08,
          "en": "So the only way of getting rid of that modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.08,
          "end": 316.4,
          "en": "is to reset error to undefined or to null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.4,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "or to any other falsy value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 322.183,
          "en": "so that this condition is no longer met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 323.6,
          "end": 326.63,
          "en": "Now to achieve this, I'll add a new function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.63,
          "end": 328.713,
          "en": "my error handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.71,
          "end": 333.21,
          "en": "which gets no argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.21,
          "end": 337.423,
          "en": "where I simply call setError and setError to null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.65999999999997,
          "end": 341.73,
          "en": "to set it from an object to null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.73,
          "end": 344.33,
          "en": "Null is treated as a falsy value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.33,
          "end": 346.523,
          "en": "so now this would no longer be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.22,
          "end": 349.21,
          "en": "Now the only question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 349.21,
          "end": 352.83,
          "en": "is how do we trigger this errorHandler function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.83,
          "end": 356.46,
          "en": "Well, I would say, from inside the ErrorModal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.46,
          "end": 358.14,
          "en": "because inside of the ErrorModal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.14,
          "end": 361.43,
          "en": "we got this button and we got the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.43,
          "end": 364.46,
          "en": "and on both we wanna register clicks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.46,
          "end": 367.303,
          "en": "and, well, trigger that error handling function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.62,
          "end": 371.41,
          "en": "So on the div here, which renders the backdrop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.41,
          "end": 373.94,
          "en": "I'll add a onClick prop which is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 373.94,
          "end": 377.74,
          "en": "on every default HTML component React offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.74,
          "end": 382.74,
          "en": "and trigger the props onConfirm function let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 384.37,
          "end": 385.96,
          "en": "Again, it's your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.96,
          "end": 387.82,
          "en": "you can name this prop whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 387.82,
          "end": 390.38,
          "en": "You can name it onHandleError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.38,
          "end": 393.98,
          "en": "or as I do it, onConfirm, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.98,
          "end": 396.92,
          "en": "The same for this button, I'll add onClick here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 396.92,
          "end": 399.09000000000003,
          "en": "and we can add onClick here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 400.86,
          "en": "because our custom button component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 400.86,
          "end": 405.36,
          "en": "which we're using, forwards whatever we pass to onClick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 405.36,
          "end": 409.25,
          "en": "to the native onClick prop hence we can add it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 409.25,
          "end": 413.34000000000003,
          "en": "And here I also wanna trigger props onConfirm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 413.34000000000003,
          "end": 415.83,
          "en": "And when I say trigger, I of course mean that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
